                  ┌──────────────────┐
                  │ RegistrationService│
                  └────────┬─────────┘
                           │
          ┌────────────────┼────────────────┐
          ▼                ▼                ▼
     Enrollment          Drop          Waitlist
          │                │                │
          ▼                ▼                ▼
   Check eligibility   Free seat      FIFO Queue
          │                │                │
          ▼                ▼                ▼
   Check capacity ───► Promote first eligible
          │
     ┌────┴────┐
     ▼         ▼
  Enrolled   Waitlisted

6. Concurrency and Persistence

- State-changing operations are synchronized so that checking capacity and updating registration happen atomically. This prevents concurrent requests from exceeding course capacity.


7. Key Assumptions

- Only one course offering is supported.
- Prerequisite eligibility is represented by a simple boolean.
- Eligibility is checked during enrollment and promotion.
- Waitlisted learners can explicitly drop from the waitlist.
- Dropping a waitlisted learner does not trigger promotion.


8. Trade-offs
- Map and Queue because the assignment is small and bounded. But data is lost when the application stops.
- When promoting, we may scan the queue until we find an eligible learner.Promotion can be O(n), but the implementation stays simple and is completely reasonable for one course.
- We use synchronized methods for state-changing operations.Simple and safe for this scope, rather than introducing more complex locking/concurrent data structures.




